        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/185\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Non-IgM monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120622,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120623,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Bone marrow is characterized by &lt;&nbsp;10% clonal involvement by neoplastic cells that are light chain&ndash;restricted on immunostaining or flow cytometry. The neoplastic cells exhibit lymphoplasmacytoid or plasma cell differentiation. They have a typical immunophenotype, including surface&nbsp;IgM+, CD5+/&minus;, CD10&minus;, CD19+, CD20+, and CD23&minus;, that would satisfactorily exclude other lymphoproliferative disorders, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120624,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120625,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>A recurrent mutation, <em>MYD88</em> p.L265P, that has been found in &gt;&nbsp;90% of patients with Waldenstr&ouml;m macroglobulinaemia (lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma), can also be present at the MGUS stage.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120626,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> serum M&nbsp;protein of &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;g/dL; &lt;&nbsp;10% bone marrow infiltration by clonal neoplastic cells; no evidence of anaemia, constitutional symptoms, hyperviscosity, lymphadenopathy, or hepatosplenomegaly that can be attributed to the underlying lymphoproliferative disorder (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/63/184/31669\" target=\"_blank\">#31669</a>Box&nbsp;4.04).</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-21T14:53:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120627,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/185\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Non-IgM monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120628,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The risk of progression of IgM MGUS to Waldenstr&ouml;m macroglobulinaemia (lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma) or a related malignancy is approximately 1.5% per year. This risk persists indefinitely {29342381}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T11:56:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]